<http://data.europa.eu/a4g/resource/0458e0c0-e4bd-4ac8-94b9-16d08667d4b2-01/Procedure/bea990b3-d02d-4129-940f-a260b01072bf>
  a epo:Procedure;
  epo:foreseesTerm <http://data.europa.eu/a4g/resource/0458e0c0-e4bd-4ac8-94b9-16d08667d4b2-01/ProcurementProjectContractTerm$_ContractAwardNotice1_ProcurementProject1>,
    <http://data.europa.eu/a4g/resource/0458e0c0-e4bd-4ac8-94b9-16d08667d4b2-01/ProcurementProjectContractTerm$_ContractAwardNotice1_ProcurementProject1_RealizedLocation1>;
  epo:hasAdditionalInformation """Access to Tender documents

Gasunie tenders are conducted entirely online via the Ariba system. Suppliers shall submit all requested information regarding the tender via Ariba.
Suppliers will gain access to the tender, after the Gasunie Procurement Desk (procurementdesk@gasunie.nl) has added the suppliers to the tender. After addition, the supplier will receive an invitation by email from the Ariba system.

If supplier would like to receive access to a tender, a request can be sent to procurementdesk@gasunie.nl.
In the case of a tender that has been announced via TenderNed, the email address of the Gasunie buyer/contact person is stated in I.1 of the announcement.

For a request for access to a tender, please send an email to procurementdesk@gasunie.nl stating the following information:

The tender name
The following company information:
- name
- street
- postal code
- city country
- AN number * (if you already have an Ariba Network account that you want to use for this tender)
The following information of the person that must be invited to the tender:
- name
- email address
- phone number
* The AN number can be found in the account settings of your Ariba Network account. Log in to your account and click on your initials at the top right to open the account settings. You can also request the Ariba Network account administrator of your organization to provide you the AN number.
If you do not have an Ariba account yet, you can register one for free via the registration link in the invitation email you receive from us.

Gasunie will send the designated person an invitation to the event as soon as possible.

If supplier have not received an invitation after two working days, please contact the Gasunie buyer/contact person again and send an email to procurementdesk@gasunie.nl."""@en;
  epo:hasInternalIdentifier <http://data.europa.eu/a4g/resource/0458e0c0-e4bd-4ac8-94b9-16d08667d4b2-01/Procedure/Identifier/WS4119242621>;
  epo:hasLegalBasis <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/legal-basis/32014L0025>;
  epo:hasProcedureType <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/procurement-procedure-type/neg-w-call>;
  epo:hasProcurementScopeDividedIntoLot <http://data.europa.eu/a4g/resource/0458e0c0-e4bd-4ac8-94b9-16d08667d4b2-01/Lot/LOT-0000>;
  epo:hasPurpose <http://data.europa.eu/a4g/resource/0458e0c0-e4bd-4ac8-94b9-16d08667d4b2-01/ProcedurePurpose$_ContractAwardNotice1_ProcurementProject1>;
  epo:isAccelerated false;
  dct:description """General Pipeline Integrity Management support services for the Gasunie offshore pipeline between Bacton (UK) and Balgzand (NL). The Service Provider provides advice and support to Gasunie in 
order to guarantee the integrity of the offshore pipe line between Bacton (UK) and Balgzand (NL). The provided support and advice will take 
place in collaboration with Gasunie and specialist third parties contracted by Gasunie. Said collaboration is to be coordinated by the service provider. In case measures are to be taken to safeguard the integrity of the pipeline
these measures shall be aligned with these third parties and integrally proposed to Gasunie."""@en;
  dct:title "Integrity Management Support Services for Gasunie subsea pipeline (Southern North Sea)"@en;
  adms:identifier <http://data.europa.eu/a4g/resource/0458e0c0-e4bd-4ac8-94b9-16d08667d4b2-01/Procedure/Identifier/bea990b3-d02d-4129-940f-a260b01072bf> .

